{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And you shall make a parapet for your roof.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): it warns that a person should guard himself from danger, in the manner of what is written (Deuteronomy 4:9): ״השמר לך ושמור נפשך מאד״ — 'Take heed to yourself and guard your soul greatly.' Therefore it commands that when he builds his house he shall make a parapet for his roof and not leave in his domain harm or an obstacle through which people might stumble, and not bring bloodguilt into his house. And similar to this is one who sets loose a vicious dog, or one who sets up a rickety ladder inside his house — and so the Sages, of blessed memory, mentioned. כי יפול הנופל — 'when the faller falls' — perhaps he will fall." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: ״ועשית מעקה לגגך כי יפול הנופל ממנו״ — 'And you shall make a parapet for your roof, when the faller falls from it' — he was worthy to fall from the six days of Creation, but you shall not be the cause that his death come through you. And the meaning of this Midrash is that all the created beings, all of them, were created with their consent and will, and the Holy One, blessed be He, informed them at the beginning of creation of all their affairs without exception, and all the events destined to come upon them; and so He informed them of the days of their lives and of their death, how it would be; and likewise the matter of their sustenance — whether in ease or in suffering, whether through themselves or through others. And so the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded: כל מעשה בראשית לדעתם נבראו לדעתם נבראו — 'all the works of Creation were created with their knowledge, with their knowledge they were created' — as it is said (Genesis 2:1–2): ״וכל צבאם״ — 'and all their host' — and all accepted and consented. And upon this they said: he was worthy to fall from the six days of Creation. Nevertheless there is great punishment for one who brings it about, and therefore: ״ועשית מעקה לגגך״ — 'And you shall make a parapet for your roof.'" "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: ״ועשית מעקה לגגך״ — 'And you shall make a parapet for your roof.' After mentioning in the sending of the mother bird (shilluach ha-ken) the Understanding (binah), which is the mother of the seven sons she raised, it was necessary to mention in this commandment the Fear (yir'ah) and the Wisdom (chochmah) that cleave to her, in order to complete all ten. For the parapet (ma'akeh) is a thing that surrounds and encompasses, and it is a supernal source — holy it is in Wisdom (chochmah) and in Understanding (binah) and in Knowledge (da'at). And the roof spread over the house is the Wisdom; and therefore the roof needs a parapet, so that it not separate and be cut — for ״ראשית חכמה יראת ה׳״ — 'the beginning of Wisdom is the fear of YHWH.' And this is ten and not nine; for were it not so, he would bring bloodguilt into the house of YHWH and bring guilt upon his soul by endangering himself. And he would surely fall from his level and stumble in his attainment — this is ״כי יפול הנופל ממנו״ — 'when the faller falls from it' — and it did not say 'lest he fall' (פן יפול), for he would surely fall from there since there is no parapet. Or one may say: ״כי יפול הנופל ממנו״ — 'when the faller falls from it' — כי יפול, 'when he falls,' כמו הנופל ממנו, 'like the one who falls from it' — alluding to Elisha ben Avuyah, after he fell and cut the shoots. And even though he did not fall from that very same place — for his cutting was below — nevertheless everything is called cutting, whether below or above."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:18.495634743Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}